# Implementation Plan - Industrial Upload Recovery & Live Extraction Visibility

The goal is to fix the 114MB upload failure (stuck at 0%) caused by Cloudflare's 100MB limit and to complete the "Extraction Chunk" visibility so the user can see real data as it is being processed.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Cloudflare 100MB Limit:** The 114.2MB file exceeds Cloudflare's default limit. We will implement **Chunked Uploads** (sending the file in 10MB parts) to bypass this restriction without needing to change your server or Cloudflare settings.

> [!NOTE]
> **Live Extraction:** We will implement a "Peeking" mechanism where the system extracts the first few rows of every table *while it is still restoring*, allowing you to see the data in the UI almost immediately after the upload finishes.

## Proposed Changes

---

### [Component] Frontend (Next.js)

We need to modify the upload logic to slice the file into chunks and send them sequentially.

#### [MODIFY] [lib/api.ts](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/apps/web/src/lib/api.ts)
- Add `uploadChunk` function to handle part-by-part uploading.
- Update `uploadDump` to use the chunking logic.

#### [MODIFY] [components/UploadCard.tsx](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/apps/web/src/components/UploadCard.tsx)
- Enhance the progress bar to handle the multi-request flow smoothly.

---

### [Component] Backend (FastAPI)

We need a way to receive and reassemble chunks on the server.

#### [MODIFY] [router.py](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/apps/api/router.py)
- Add a NEW endpoint `/upload/chunk` to receive file slices.
- Modify the `/upload` completion logic to trigger the pipeline once all chunks are merged.

---

### [Component] Extraction Pipeline

Enhance the "Industrial Visibility" to show real data chunks.

#### [MODIFY] [service.py (DumpRestore)](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/services/dump_restore/service.py)
- Update the `_flush_progress` (heartbeat) to query the first 5 rows of each discovered table in the `staging` schema.
- Store these "chunks" in the `Job.profile` JSON.

#### [MODIFY] [TableView.tsx](file:///home/eisen/Downloads/SQAuto/apps/web/src/components/TableView.tsx)
- Update the UI to subscribe to these live profile updates and render the "Extracted Chunks" immediately.

---

## Open Questions

- **Cloudflare Tunnels:** Are you using a Cloudflare Tunnel or just the standard Proxy? (Chunked uploads solve both, but good to know).
- **Table Priority:** Should we prioritize extracting specific tables first if they are found?

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Upload a generated 120MB file to verify the chunking works beyond the 100MB limit.
- Verify that `is_compressed` logic still correctly identifies `.sql.gz` chunks after reassembly.

### Manual Verification
- Watch the Dashboard after a 114MB upload to see if the "Extracted Tables" cards populate with real row samples *before* the entire 1.8GB restore is finished.
